{{!
	PinnableHeader: the visible header row of a pinnable region -- the region's label plus the
	two toggle affordances that move it between its pinned (column) and unpinned (dropdown)
	placements. A leaf partial: it includes no other partial. Its only consumer is
	PinnableElement/Open.mustache, which invokes it inside its data-pinnable-header section, so
	the keys below are read from that nested object rather than from the page-level data.

	Data dictionary supplied by NotionComponentPinnableHeader::getTemplateData():
	bool is-pinned whether the region currently sits in its pinned placement. It selects the
		third wrapper class -- notion-pinnable-header-pinned or notion-pinnable-header-unpinned --
		and nothing else. Both buttons are always emitted so the header is complete and correct
		before any script runs, and components/PinnableHeader.less keys off that state class to
		reveal exactly one of them: never both, never neither.
	string label the region's human readable name, already resolved from the id-derived
		message, e.g. `Contents`.
	string label-tag-name element name for the label, `div` by default and a heading where the
		label is semantically a heading (the pinnable table of contents promotes it). It is
		interpolated into BOTH the opening and the closing tag so the two can never disagree. A
		non-empty tag name is the component's contract -- its constructor defaults to `div` --
		because a dynamic tag name cannot be guarded without duplicating the whole element.
	string pin-label visible text of the pin button, e.g. `move to sidebar`.
	string unpin-label visible text of the unpin button, e.g. `hide`.
	string pin-aria-label accessible name of the pin button: the parameterised form that names
		the region, e.g. `Move Contents to sidebar`. Deliberately richer than the visible text,
		which reads as an instruction only in the context of the header it sits in.
	string unpin-aria-label accessible name of the unpin button, e.g. `Hide Contents`.
	string data-pinnable-element-id id of the pinnable region, e.g. `notion-toc`. Woven into
		four places here -- the second wrapper class, the data attribute of the same name and
		both analytics event names -- so a single wrong value breaks pinning for that one region
		while every other region keeps working.
	string data-feature-name feature key WITHOUT the `notion-` prefix, e.g. `toc-pinned`.
	string data-pinned-container-id id of the pinned mount point, the region id suffixed with
		`-pinned-container`.
	string data-unpinned-container-id id of the unpinned mount point, the region id suffixed
		with `-unpinned-container`.

	The four data-* attributes are a runtime contract with resources/skins.notion.js and its
	pinnableElement.js and features.js: the feature name drives the stored user preference and
	the document classes, while the element and container ids are resolved with
	document.getElementById to relocate the region. Each attribute is guarded by its own section
	so an absent value emits no empty attribute -- that script warns and aborts on an empty one
	rather than moving a region to nowhere -- and the toggle-button class is carried by both
	buttons because the script binds them together, while the unpin button additionally carries
	its own class as the post-toggle focus target. data-event-name carries the analytics event,
	whose `pinnable-header.` prefix is a shared event namespace and so is NOT skin-prefixed.

	Every interpolation is escaped: this partial emits no raw HTML, applies no inline style and
	performs no message lookup. A wrong label is therefore fixed in
	NotionComponentPinnableHeader.php or in i18n/en.json, never here.
}}
<div
	class="notion-pinnable-header {{data-pinnable-element-id}}-pinnable-header notion-pinnable-header-{{#is-pinned}}pinned{{/is-pinned}}{{^is-pinned}}unpinned{{/is-pinned}}"
	{{#data-feature-name}}data-feature-name="{{.}}"{{/data-feature-name}}
	{{#data-pinnable-element-id}}data-pinnable-element-id="{{.}}"{{/data-pinnable-element-id}}
	{{#data-pinned-container-id}}data-pinned-container-id="{{.}}"{{/data-pinned-container-id}}
	{{#data-unpinned-container-id}}data-unpinned-container-id="{{.}}"{{/data-unpinned-container-id}}
>
	<{{label-tag-name}} class="notion-pinnable-header-label">{{label}}</{{label-tag-name}}>
	<button class="notion-pinnable-header-toggle-button notion-pinnable-header-pin-button" data-event-name="pinnable-header.{{data-pinnable-element-id}}.pin" aria-label="{{pin-aria-label}}">{{pin-label}}</button>
	<button class="notion-pinnable-header-toggle-button notion-pinnable-header-unpin-button" data-event-name="pinnable-header.{{data-pinnable-element-id}}.unpin" aria-label="{{unpin-aria-label}}">{{unpin-label}}</button>
</div>
